<title>UK: UK M4 grows provisional 9.6 pct in year to Dec.</title>
<headline>UK M4 grows provisional 9.6 pct in year to Dec.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England published the following data on UK monetary aggregates for Dec -</p>
<p>    MONEY SUPPLY				    Dec	    Nov*</p>
<p>    M4 in month	  (adjusted)	     -0.2	  1.1</p>
<p>	 in year to date (adjusted)		9.6	 10.8</p>
<p>    M4 in month	(unadjusted)		unch	 1.6</p>
<p>	 in year to date (unadjusted)	    9.5	 10.7</p>
<p>Adjusted lending by banks, building</p>
<p>    societies in billions of stg		 -3.8	 7.0</p>
<p>NOTE - consensus forecasts M4 +10.8 pct yr/yr, M4 lending +6.3 billion stg. * Previously published final figures for Nov</p>
<p>    Three-month annual M4 rate (adj)	   8.0</p>
<p>    Six-month annual M4 rate   (adj)	   9.2</p>
<p>-- LONDON NEWSROOM ++44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
